  "notes": "Lafayette Avenue: name printed only on the curved 40 ft part east of the fork at 6110,3383; the street running west from there across Clifton Avenue (and west of it) has no name printed in the strip and is taken as Lafayette Avenue. Lafayette Circle: 'CIRCLE' is printed on the east arc; the branch going south-east from the fork runs smoothly into the loop, so it is taken as Lafayette Circle; the loop rejoins Lafayette Avenue where Marjorie Avenue starts (6790,3585; three-way). Ringwalt: suffix not seen in the strip, Avenue assumed. Belsaw Place (letters spaced across the block, read BELSAW PLACE): a private loop ('Lot A', 40 ft on the north, west and south legs, about 20 ft on the east leg); its south leg reaches Clifton Avenue at 5387,4927 and a narrow lane with a 6 in. water pipe runs north from the east leg and then east to Clifton Avenue at 5375,4385 (doubtful as a street). Unnamed '?' at 7100,4910: a 50 ft street running south from Dell Eva Lane to a dead end and curving north-east past the east end of Severn Avenue. Unnamed '?' at x 7108 between Juergens Avenue (corner, 7108,5743) and Greendale Avenue: 50 ft, may be the turn of Juergens Avenue. 'STEP' printed between lots north of Severn Avenue at x 6695: steps, not a street. Private drive east of Clifton Avenue near 6600,2000 not picked. Egbert Avenue above the bend at 4905,1190 has no crossings."
